"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPageViewStyle(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":". The style defines the page indicator colors, as well as how page content fades out above the page indicator.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Apply ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingPageViewContentFade()","type":"reference"},{"text":" to scrolling page content, like a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScrollView"},{"text":", to fade it out before it reaches the page indicator. Screens like ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingIntroScreen"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingWhatsNewScreen","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" already do this."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Slideshow","anchor":"Slideshow"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshow","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" presents pages that automatically progress after a certain duration, like a story. It shows a progress bar for each page at the top of the view, and calls "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onStoryCompleted"},{"type":"text","text":" when the last page has been presented."}]},{"type":"row","columns":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"OnboardingSlideshow","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"size":1},{"content":[{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["OnboardingSlideshow(","    state: state,","    onStoryCompleted: { dismiss() },","    content: { page in","        OnboardingPageContent {","            Text(\"Slide \\(page.pageIndex + 1)\")","        }","    },","    bottomButtons: { state in","        OnboardingPrimaryButton(state.isLastPage ? \"Done\" : \"Next\") {","            withAnimation {","                state.showNextPage(orDismiss: dismiss)","            }","        }","    }",")",".onboardingSlideshowConfiguration(...)",".onboardingSlideshowStyle(...)"]}],"size":3}],"numberOfColumns":4},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The user can tap a progress bar to jump to a certain page. On iOS and visionOS, the user can also tap the left and right side of a slide to move back and forth, and long press to pause the slideshow."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A slideshow can be configured with an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshowConfiguration","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which is applied with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingSlideshowConfiguration(_:)","isActive":true},{"text":". It defines the slide duration, the progress timer tick increment, and the accessibility labels of the tap areas.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A slideshow can be styled with an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshowStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":", which is applied with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/onboardingSlideshowStyle(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":". It defines the colors and height of the progress bars, which are rendered with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.OnboardingKit\/documentation\/OnboardingKit\/OnboardingSlideshowProgressView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"